  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Latakia Wildfire Crisis Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam activated the immediate response to the affected population in close coordination with the local authorities. According to the operation room, most of the organizations are supporting with water trucking, fuel provision, human resources, food, safety, and hygiene kits for the civil defense working in the firefighting.  As of now, the electrical substation transformer of Ra&apos;s al -Basit is damaged and burned. This substation provides electricity to several water pumping stations. So far, 4 water pumping stations have been damaged. However, there is no official report quantifying the total infrastructure damage, which limits precise planning. Field assessments are suspended, and when possible they will resume in order to identify installation points and coordinate efforts with the Lattakia water establishment.</narrative>
  </description>
